Subject: [PATCH 2/2] libexec/mail: Refuse to deliver what is not mail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: ssysnkqupvyyyutpqwnkmtprurvtlmtt
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:40:42 +0000

maildir-deliver.sh filed whatever arrived on stdin into the list
maildir. An empty file, command output, or a draft missing its
headers became a list message, and the mistake surfaced only after it
was posted. Once git send-email hands it messages as its sendmail
program, it is the one gate every message passes, so it should accept
only a well-formed message.

From, Subject, and Message-ID are required because the list cannot
use a message without them: it is unattributed, untitled, or
unthreadable. The check runs before the message leaves tmp/, so a
refused message never reaches the maildir.

Add the first tests for libexec/mail.
